{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is written 100% in "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the highest quality generics, constraints, and interfaces to make sure the library and your projects are as type-safe as possible!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"infer-form-and-field-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infer form and field types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form works out your form's data type from its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":". From\nthere, each field name points to a value in that data shape, so field callbacks\nand form methods know which values belong at each path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Don't write the full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormApi"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldApi"},{"type":"text","value":" generic parameter lists by hand in\napplication code. Those signatures may change as TanStack Form's type\ninference evolves. At component boundaries, use the adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*FormType"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldWithValue<T>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFieldApi"},{"type":"text","value":", or the adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Any*FormApi"},{"type":"text","value":" helper,\ndepending on what the component needs. The "},{"type":"link","href":"./splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nguide shows how to use each helper."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"compiler-requirements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compiler requirements"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict: true"},{"type":"text","value":" in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsconfig.json"},{"type":"text","value":" so TypeScript can check field\npaths, values, and callbacks as intended. TanStack Form's types require\nTypeScript 5.4 or later."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-changes-between-releases","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type changes between releases"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Improvements and corrections to TanStack Form's types may ship in patch\nreleases. These changes don't affect runtime behaviour, but they may reveal a\ntype error in application code that previously compiled."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need to plan for those updates, pin your TanStack Form adapter to an\nexact patch version and review any new type errors when upgrading. Changes to\nthe runtime API continue to follow semantic versioning."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"infer-form-and-field-types","text":"Infer form and field types","level":2},{"id":"compiler-requirements","text":"Compiler requirements","level":2},{"id":"type-changes-between-releases","text":"Type changes between releases","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is written 100% in **TypeScript** with the highest quality generics, constraints, and interfaces to make sure the library and your projects are as type-safe as possible!\n\n## Infer form and field types\n\nTanStack Form works out your form's data type from its `defaultValues`. From\nthere, each field name points to a value in that data shape, so field callbacks\nand form methods know which values belong at each path.\n\nDon't write the full `FormApi` or `FieldApi` generic parameter lists by hand in\napplication code. Those signatures may change as TanStack Form's type\ninference evolves. At component boundaries, use the adapter's `*FormType`,\n`FieldWithValue<T>`, `AnyFieldApi`, or the adapter's `Any*FormApi` helper,\ndepending on what the component needs. The [Splitting forms](./splitting-forms)\nguide shows how to use each helper.\n\n## Compiler requirements\n\nEnable `strict: true` in your `tsconfig.json` so TypeScript can check field\npaths, values, and callbacks as intended. TanStack Form's types require\nTypeScript 5.4 or later.\n\n## Type changes between releases\n\nImprovements and corrections to TanStack Form's types may ship in patch\nreleases. These changes don't affect runtime behaviour, but they may reveal a\ntype error in application code that previously compiled.\n\nIf you need to plan for those updates, pin your TanStack Form adapter to an\nexact patch version and review any new type errors when upgrading. Changes to\nthe runtime API continue to follow semantic versioning.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: typescript\ntitle: TypeScript\n---\n\nTanStack Form is written 100% in **TypeScript** with the highest quality generics, constraints, and interfaces to make sure the library and your projects are as type-safe as possible!\n\n## Infer form and field types\n\nTanStack Form works out your form's data type from its `defaultValues`. From\nthere, each field name points to a value in that data shape, so field callbacks\nand form methods know which values belong at each path.\n\nDon't write the full `FormApi` or `FieldApi` generic parameter lists by hand in\napplication code. Those signatures may change as TanStack Form's type\ninference evolves. At component boundaries, use the adapter's `*FormType`,\n`FieldWithValue<T>`, `AnyFieldApi`, or the adapter's `Any*FormApi` helper,\ndepending on what the component needs. The [Splitting forms](./splitting-forms)\nguide shows how to use each helper.\n\n## Compiler requirements\n\nEnable `strict: true` in your `tsconfig.json` so TypeScript can check field\npaths, values, and callbacks as intended. TanStack Form's types require\nTypeScript 5.4 or later.\n\n## Type changes between releases\n\nImprovements and corrections to TanStack Form's types may ship in patch\nreleases. These changes don't affect runtime behaviour, but they may reveal a\ntype error in application code that previously compiled.\n\nIf you need to plan for those updates, pin your TanStack Form adapter to an\nexact patch version and review any new type errors when upgrading. Changes to\nthe runtime API continue to follow semantic versioning.\n"}
